[{"id":2770545864,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6lIyzI","state":"APPROVED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?u=96b5dc9be2859dca5f31314c87d99a68a21e1576&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","login":"BastiaanOlij","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij"},"body":"@mbucchia  Sorry it took me awhile to get to this and properly test it.\r\n\r\nFunctionally this is working great for me. I've tested it both with the demo project on my original issue and running OpenXR with DX12 over SteamVR.\r\n\r\nTechnically I'm going to trust that the DX12 implementation is sound. My only question is whether you added the `d3d12_hooks` logic because Vulkan had it, or if it actually is used? None of the methods are implemented so I think you can leave this out. \r\nIn Vulkan this is required because we let OpenXR handle the Vulkan instance creation, but I don't think that is required for DX.\r\n\r\nRegarding the issue around WMR mentioned in the original issue. I think we can ignore this. With WMR basically defunct and no longer available in Windows 11, adding any sort of workaround in the code is daft. If someone really still wants to work with WMR on Windows 10, they can follow the instructions on the issue and do a custom build of Godot.\r\n\r\n@clayjohn might want to have a quick check on the DX code but I think this is pretty much good to merge depending on the answer to the hooks question.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104207#pullrequestreview-2770545864","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104207","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2025-04-16T03:25:46Z"},{"id":2688621240,"node_i